# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD boots mongod with the zlib-enabled config using --fork and
# then execs `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * the daemon is ALREADY RUNNING (advertising zlib) when the agent starts,
#     which is what makes the "edited mongod.conf but never restarted" case
#     detectable via the live isMaster/hello compressor list;
#   * PID 1 is still `sleep infinity`, so restarting mongod cannot kill the
#     container.
#
# Consequence for solutions: a fix must RESTART mongod, not merely edit the
# config file — the running server keeps negotiating zlib until it is restarted.
